1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(New bonus scenes)

2
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,420
(Busy even on the way to investigate)

3
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,430
What are you doing?

4
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:11,710
It's too heavy.

5
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:13,260
(Taking off gear)

6
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,510
He's like this every day.

7
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:16,000
(I know him too well)
He does really weird stuff.

8
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,340
(The belt's too heavy)

9
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:20,270
(Too much stuff)
I wanna take my jacket off too.

10
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,980
Is there anything to eat?

11
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,430
(Looking for food)
There's nothing.

12
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,910
What happened to this cake?

13
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:25,610
Who did this?

14
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:26,160
No idea.

15
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:26,970
It was like this when I got here.

16
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:27,910
Its head fell off.

17
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:28,670
Yeah, it was like that.

18
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:29,630
It was already headless.

19
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:30,950
Maybe it's a clue.

20
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,430
(Serious analysis)
What if the cake

21
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:34,240
was supposed to look like this.

22
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:36,470
(Showcasing his true skills)
Or it sat too long and melted.

23
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:39,150
That makes sense.

24
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,620
(He's got a point)
Maybe it started out...

25
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,060
(Gets icing all over his hand)

26
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,140
Go wash your hands.

27
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:44,330
Go wash them.

28
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:45,220
There's tissue here.

29
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:45,900
Okay.

30
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:46,750
Thanks.

31
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:47,630
I'll use it later.

32
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,350
It was made like this.

33
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:49,700
Yeah.

34
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,110
(Definitely overthinking it)
It couldn't hold itself up anymore.

35
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:51,990
You're right.

36
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,870
It melted.

37
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:53,680
It melted on its own.

38
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,950
It just flopped.

39
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:58,870
Why don't you introduce yourself later

40
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,070
(Self-intro time)
and tell us what you do.

41
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:00,610
Okay.

42
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,110
Just your job and your name.

43
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:02,820
Let's go.

44
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:03,380
Okay.

45
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:05,550
It's pouring again.

46
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:06,110
It's raining again.

47
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,790
Who's gonna protect me?

48
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:08,640
I will.

49
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:11,740
(Humming in the rain)
♪A summer evening after the rain♪

50
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:12,480
♪ I always♪

51
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,090
Here, cover yourself.

52
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:15,440
We've got an umbrella.

53
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:16,590
It's only a few steps. Let's go.

54
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,030
I've got dye in my hair.

55
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,550
I don't wanna ruin it.

56
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,750
Fine, use the umbrella.

57
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,220
We're going back again.

58
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:23,770
Why did we even come all the way?

59
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,430
I'm innocent.

60
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:27,720
You don't even need to check my room.

61
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:28,880
(Start exploring)
Where's He's room?

62
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,030
Here. Second floor.

63
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,350
Is this my room?

64
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:32,770
Upstairs.

65
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:35,230
It's open.

66
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:36,310
(Fearless)
She's got guts.

67
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,230
Come on.

68
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:38,990
What's his name?

69
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:39,500
He's here.

70
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,390
I'm He Struggle.

71
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:45,480
What about Jin Goofy, He Struggle
and Ke Uh-Oh?

72
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:46,070
Wait.

73
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,550
(Always on alert)
Can someone check that plant?

74
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,590
The last one.

75
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,390
See if there's anything inside it.

76
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,100
(Sniffer dog mode)
Any meal cards in there?

77
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:52,630
Why do I feel like

78
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,350
(Detective instinct kicking in)
there's something in this plant?

79
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:55,640
A key clue.

80
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:56,260
Exactly.

81
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:58,150
There's another plant there.

82
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,230
Ding, straight ahead.

83
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,290
(Fox detective on it)

84
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,730
Seriously, there are only
a few episodes left.

85
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:05,450
There aren't many chances left
to become a legend.

86
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:08,570
(No clues found)
Nothing.

87
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:09,300
Nothing.

88
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:10,960
Just give up.

89
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,750
There's no way we can find

90
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,830
"key evidence".

91
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:17,140
(Daily chatter)

92
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,890
Leave the umbrella outside, Nan.

93
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:19,650
Okay.

94
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:21,070
Take your umbrella.

95
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:21,830
I need to wash my hands.

96
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:25,180
(Both scrambling around)

97
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,040
Wait.

98
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,680
No.

99
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:29,240
(Let me do it)
Like this.

100
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:30,870
Good thing we've got security.

101
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,310
Quick, the bucket is almost full.

102
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,110
Hurry up and wash.

103
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:35,070
Come on.

104
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:35,750
Am I...

105
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,670
(Something feels off)
the cleaner here?

106
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,910
Can we turn it off now?

107
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:39,450
Where do I turn it off?

108
00:02:39,450 --> 00:02:40,060
How?

109
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:40,740
Okay.

110
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:42,460
(Capybara needs to recharge)

111
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,900
I'm gonna wash up.

112
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:45,420
(Line up to wash hands)

113
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,590
Capybara.

114
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:52,790
Capybara.

115
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,380
(Singing along)
Bara-capybara.

116
00:02:55,910 --> 00:02:57,520
(Capybara over here)
Capybara.

117
00:02:58,270 --> 00:03:01,200
("Makka Pakka" over here)
Capybara.

118
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,210
Jin Goofy, I almost read your notebook.

119
00:03:03,210 --> 00:03:04,010
Hold on to it.

120
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,110
Once you see it,
you'll know I'm innocent.

121
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:06,750
Go on, look.

122
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:07,270
(Your Honor)
Seriously?

123
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:07,760
Yeah.

124
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,260
Stop pretending.

125
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:10,240
Everyone knows the killer's notebook

126
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,710
wouldn't just be left here.

127
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,740
Who hasn't played the killer before?

128
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:14,360
(Already figured it out)
Who hasn't been the killer before?

129
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,050
What do you mean?

130
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:16,980
(New here)
Nan Shy, wait.

131
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,050
Hold this.

132
00:03:18,050 --> 00:03:18,740
We've got loads to ask you.

133
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,010
You're in for a tough one.

134
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:20,820
Exactly.

135
00:03:20,820 --> 00:03:21,400
Okay.

136
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,560
(Not worried at all)
You got my notebook soaked.

137
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,550
Are we eating soon? I'm starving.

138
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,310
(Stomach growling)
Isn't it lunchtime?

139
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,590
Almost.

140
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:31,080
We're always like this.

141
00:03:31,290 --> 00:03:32,480
We usually don't even eat.

142
00:03:32,490 --> 00:03:33,990
(Nonsense)
We never eat on days off.

143
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,590
Once you finish discussing
at the workplace,

144
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:38,590
then you can eat.

145
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,270
We're discussing here?

146
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:39,650
Awesome.

147
00:03:39,650 --> 00:03:39,870
Let's go.

148
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:40,310
(Food time)
Let's go.

149
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:48,500
(Checking everyone's animal identity)

150
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,350
(Suggestion)
Why don't we test one by one?

151
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,150
I'll go.

152
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:52,050
(Me first)
Come on, move.

153
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,390
Let the bunny try first.

154
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,860
(Recognition failed)

155
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:56,470
(Making it up)
There, it worked.

156
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,150
See?

157
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,670
(Gets it immediately)
Bunny.

158
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,710
(This is too much)
Stop making fun of her bunny teeth.

159
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,400
It really didn't work.

160
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,290
Your turn, Jin.

161
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,230
Jin, try it.

162
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:08,620
(Expressive)

163
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,750
That's obviously a human.

164
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,830
(Love it)
So pretty.

165
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,150
Okay, done.

166
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,110
You can get off now.

167
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:14,480
Your turn.

168
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,710
You killer.

169
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,220
(Why don't you try?)

170
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:22,270
(Recognition failed)
You're human too.

171
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:22,590
No way.

172
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,710
(Confused)
Haven't you already grown capybara fur?

173
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,190
Next.

174
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,150
Ke, you go.

175
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:29,070
There must be two types.

176
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,510
(Logical mode)
One turns animals into humans,

177
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,070
and one turns humans into animals.

178
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,250
We're human.

179
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:34,250
Yeah, we're human.

180
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,300
Next.

181
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,870
Do we even need to check?

182
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:40,100
(I'll try anyway)

183
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:41,620
(Recognition failed)

184
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:42,350
Nothing.

185
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,670
Will it recognize me?

186
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,790
(Failed the test)
I'm human.

187
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:48,340
(Tries stretching)

188
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:50,860
(Recognition failed)

189
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:53,110
Anyone left?

190
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:54,340
Nope.

191
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:55,940
There are only six of us.

192
00:04:56,090 --> 00:04:57,710
(All tested human)
There are six of us.

193
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:00,020
(He-pybara joins the club)

194
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,150
Night-vision goggles.

195
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,040
(Looking for clues)
Then that really rules you two out.

196
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:04,720
Yeah.

197
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:05,500
(Fair enough)

198
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,070
Since we can see,

199
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:08,020
we don't need them.

200
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:09,850
I just remembered.

201
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:11,190
(Joining them)
I'm a canine too.

202
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,430
(That's a stretch)
What kind of canine are you?

203
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,190
(One more hit)
Suddenly you're a canine now?

204
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,910
It's definitely him.

205
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,630
They never introduced his animal.

206
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,100
(Brought it on himself)

207
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,150
(Genuine question)
Wait, is a capybara actually a canine?

208
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,070
(He's messing with you)
No, he made that up.

209
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,110
It's definitely him.

210
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:27,510
(Even more convinced)
Because

211
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,150
they didn't introduce
his animal just now.

212
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,670
(We know you way too well)
Listen to him making stuff up.

213
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,350
They didn't introduce mine either.

214
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,390
You're a fish.

215
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:36,670
(Roll call) Fish, pipa, canine,
and bunny were mentioned.

216
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,390
(Only you)
Only the capybara was left out.

217
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:43,350
Don't trust her right now.

218
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,790
(Unconditional trust)
Of course I trust her.

219
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,670
So these are night-vision goggles.

220
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,630
(Searching hard)
What else is there?

221
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,030
Keep looking.

222
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,270
Are you afraid we'll find something?

223
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:52,820
(He stays completely still)

224
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:53,430
A pair of glasses.

225
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:54,510
A remote.

226
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,110
Anything else?

227
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:56,710
Nope. Anything?

228
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,390
(Not giving up)
Keep looking.

229
00:05:58,520 --> 00:05:59,730
(Back and forth)
We walked all the way back again.

230
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:01,700
(Watching you)
Capybara's gone quiet now.

231
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:03,540
Okay.

232
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:06,950
=The Truth=

233
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,070
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at 12PM.)

234
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,100
(VIP updates next day at 12PM,
one week early.)
